<div class="frr-wrap">
  <p class="frr-lead">
    Optional <strong>routing software</strong> for this Unraid host
    (<a href="https://frrouting.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FRRouting</a>).
    Use it when you need multi-hop / multipath fabrics — not for ordinary SMB on one LAN cable.
    Different from the stock <strong>Routing Table</strong> tab (simple kernel routes only).
  </p>

  <div class="frr-companion">
    <strong>Need this?</strong> Rings, multi-hop, Proxmox/Linux FRR peers, multi-node AI underlays ·
    <strong>Skip:</strong> single static Thunderbolt or Ethernet cable ·
<?php if ($tbn): ?>
    <strong>Thunderbolt Net:</strong> cable underlay + OpenFabric <em>policy</em> on
    <a href="/Settings/NetworkSettings">Network Settings → Thunderbolt</a>
    (this tab only installs packages / daemons)
<?php else: ?>
    <strong>Thunderbolt Net:</strong> optional companion for TB host-net
<?php endif; ?>
  </div>
  <details class="frr-about">
    <summary>What is FRR? (start here if new)</summary>
    <div class="frr-about-body">
      <p><strong>FRR</strong> is open-source routing software used on many Linux routers and Proxmox hosts.
      Unraid does not ship it. This plugin installs FRR packages onto your flash/RAM OS, then starts daemons you choose.</p>
      <p><strong>First-time path:</strong>
        set <em>Auto-download packages = Yes</em> → <strong>Apply</strong> (leave progress window open) →
        wait until finished → hard-refresh. After packages are cached, you can set Auto-download back to
        <em>No</em>; reboots still rehydrate from flash if <em>Install on array start</em> is Yes.</p>
      <p><strong>OpenFabric</strong> is the multi-hop fabric protocol (daemon <code>fabricd</code>).
        Thunderbolt metrics/participate live under Thunderbolt Net, not here.</p>
      <p><strong>Safe defaults:</strong> does not edit <code>br0</code> / Wi‑Fi / <code>network.cfg</code>.
        BGP/OSPF stay Off until you enable them.</p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/docs/frr-and-unraid-routing.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FRR vs Unraid routing ↗</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/docs/defaults-rationale.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Why these defaults ↗</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/DOCS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Full docs ↗</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <div class="frr-section" style="margin-top:0.35em">
    <h3>Status</h3>
    <table class="frr-status tablesorter shift">
      <tr>
        <td>Plugin</td>
        <td><code><?= $ver ?></code>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — Plugins tab updates</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Unraid product</td>
        <td><code><?= $uver ?></code> · <code><?= $arch ?></code>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — picks package bundle (not kernel)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>FRR live</td>
        <td>
<?php if ($frr_ok): ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-ok">Present</span>
          <?php if (!empty($det['version'])): ?>
            <code class="frr-muted"><?= htmlspecialchars($det['version']) ?></code>
          <?php endif; ?>
<?php else: ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-warn">Not installed</span>
          <span class="frr-muted"> — Apply to download when a bundle exists</span>
<?php endif; ?>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Daemons</td>
        <td>
          <span class="frr-badge <?= $zebra_run ? 'frr-badge-ok' : 'frr-badge-bad' ?>"><?= $zebra_run ? 'zebra up' : 'zebra down' ?></span>
          <span class="frr-badge <?= $fabricd_run ? 'frr-badge-ok' : 'frr-badge-bad' ?>"><?= $fabricd_run ? 'fabricd up' : 'fabricd down' ?></span>
          <span class="frr-muted"> · <?= htmlspecialchars($det['note'] ?? '') ?></span>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Catalog bundle</td>
        <td>
<?php if ($bundle_ok): ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-ok">Match</span>
          FRR <code><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['frr_version'] ?? '') ?></code>
          · channel <code><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['channel'] ?? '') ?></code>
<?php else: ?>
          <span class="frr-badge frr-badge-warn">No match yet</span>
          <span class="frr-muted"><?= htmlspecialchars($bundle['error'] ?? 'resolving…') ?></span>
          <br><span class="frr-muted">Hard-refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R) after catalog updates, then <strong>Apply</strong> to force re-fetch. See <a href="https://github.com/ibigsnet/UnraidFRR/blob/main/packages/SUPPORTED.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SUPPORTED.md ↗</a>.</span>
<?php endif; ?>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Flash package cache</td>
        <td><?= $pk
          ? count($pk) . ' managed file(s) — ' . htmlspecialchars(implode(', ', $pk))
          : '<span class="frr-muted">Empty — Apply auto-downloads when a catalog match exists</span>' ?></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Thunderbolt Net</td>
        <td><?= $tbn
          ? '<span class="frr-ok">Installed</span> <span class="frr-muted">— policy on Thunderbolt tab</span>'
          : '<span class="frr-muted">Not installed (OK)</span>' ?></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
    <input type="hidden" name="#file" value="UnraidFRR/UnraidFRR.cfg">
    <input type="hidden" name="#include" value="/plugins/UnraidFRR/include/frr-update.php">

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Packages</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">How FRR is downloaded and rehydrated after reboot.</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>Package channel:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="package_channel">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['package_channel'] ?? 'latest', 'latest', 'Latest stable (recommended)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['package_channel'] ?? 'latest', 'previous', 'Previous stable (rollback)') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Automated set from the project catalog. Channels appear as builds are published.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Auto-download packages:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="auto_download">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['auto_download'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No (default — flash cache only)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['auto_download'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes — fetch from catalog on Apply') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        <strong>Default No:</strong> Apply will not hit the network for large package files.
        <strong>First install:</strong> set <strong>Yes</strong>, click Apply, wait for the progress window to finish,
        then you may set No again. Later reboots use packages already on flash (see Install on array start).
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Install on array start:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="install_on_start">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['install_on_start'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (recommended)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['install_on_start'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        After reboot, reinstall packages <em>already on the flash</em> into the live (RAM) system — <strong>no download</strong>.
        Unraid’s root filesystem does not keep <code>installpkg</code> results across boot.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Catalog URL (advanced):</dt>
        <dd>
          <input type="text" name="package_base_url" style="width:min(32em,100%)"
            value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['package_base_url'] ?? '') ?>"
            placeholder="default: GitHub packages/manifest.json">
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Leave empty for the official catalog. Only change if you host a mirror.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Core daemons</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">
        These start with FRR. Leave Yes for OpenFabric multi-hop; leave optional protocols Off unless you know you need them.
      </p>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable zebra:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_zebra">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_zebra'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (required for routing)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_zebra'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        FRR’s core process — talks to the Linux kernel routing table. Almost always Yes if you use this plugin at all.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable fabricd (OpenFabric):</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_fabricd">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_fabricd'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes (multi-hop fabric)') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_fabricd'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Multi-hop fabric protocol (used with Thunderbolt rings / mixed Linux peers).
        Does not by itself put your LAN bridge into a mesh — policy is separate
        (Thunderbolt Net for TB links; advanced <code>frr.conf</code> for others).
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Enable staticd:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="enable_staticd">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_staticd'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['enable_staticd'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Lets FRR manage static routes (optional). Unraid can still own simple statics on the stock Routing Table.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="frr-section">
      <h3>Optional protocols</h3>
      <p class="frr-section-lead">Default all No — enable only what you use (not needed for OpenFabric/TB alone).</p>
      <div class="frr-daemon-grid">
        <label>bgpd
          <select name="enable_bgpd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bgpd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bgpd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>ospfd
          <select name="enable_ospfd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospfd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospfd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>ospf6d
          <select name="enable_ospf6d"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospf6d'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_ospf6d'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>isisd
          <select name="enable_isisd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_isisd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_isisd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
        <label>bfdd
          <select name="enable_bfdd"><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bfdd'] ?? 'no', 'no', 'No') ?><?= mk_option($cfg['enable_bfdd'] ?? 'no', 'yes', 'Yes') ?></select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        Advanced FRR protocols. Leave No unless you deliberately run BGP/OSPF/IS-IS/BFD on this host.
      </blockquote>

      <dl>
        <dt>Start/restart FRR on Apply:</dt>
        <dd>
          <select name="start_frr">
            <?= mk_option($cfg['start_frr'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', 'Yes') ?>
            <?= mk_option($cfg['start_frr'] ?? 'yes', 'no', 'No') ?>
          </select>
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <blockquote class="inline_help">
        After download/install, bring the FRR service up (or reload) so daemons match the checkboxes above.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="frr-actions">
      <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="Apply">
      <input type="button" value="Done" onclick="done()">
    </div>
    <p class="frr-muted" style="margin:0.65em 0 0;font-size:0.9em;line-height:1.4">
      <strong>Apply</strong> opens Unraid’s progress window (like other Settings saves).
      <strong>Do not close it</strong> until it shows finished — especially if Auto-download is Yes (large packages).
      Only one Apply runs at a time. Then hard-refresh this page (Ctrl+Shift+R).
    </p>
  </form>
</div>
